#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Change tasks: an agent adds, renames, removes or implements code across a real repository, and
hidden acceptance tests decide whether it did. Measures tokens, turns, wall time and success per
arm, and how the agent navigated (graph calls against grep, glob and file reads).

    bench/agent-loop/change-tasks --list
    bench/agent-loop/change-tasks --task petclinic-owner-email --arm jk --runs 1
    bench/agent-loop/change-tasks --arm jk --arm jk-hooks --arm mvn --runs 5
    bench/agent-loop/change-tasks --driver grok --arm jk --arm jk-hooks
    bench/agent-loop/change-tasks --render [--out DIR]

Tasks are in tasks.toml; each task's hidden files are under tasks/<task>/ and are copied over the
sandbox only after the agent stops. Repositories are the graph-retrieval corpus
(bench/graph-retrieval/repos.toml), set up there with `bench setup`. Sandboxes and transcripts
live under $AGENT_LOOP_HOME/change-tasks/<date>/. README.md section "Change tasks" says what the
arms are.
"""

